Path("docs/terminal/INTERACTIVE_TERMINAL_UX.md").write_text('''# Interactive terminal UX (P08-007)\n\n## Scope\n\n`FCCD-P08-007` composes the existing typed ConPTY host into the Bottom Tool Panel terminal seam. It does not replace the P08-004 process ownership boundary and does not claim the P08-008 final process/terminal safety convergence task.\n\n## User surface\n\n- PowerShell and Command Prompt are resolved from Windows system paths.\n- Git Bash and WSL appear only when the read-only optional-shell detector reports a verified installation.\n- Start/Close controls make lifecycle ownership explicit.\n- UTF-8 text input and output are streamed through `IConPtyTerminalSession`; the UI never bypasses that boundary with `Process.Start` or shell command-string execution.\n- Ctrl+C copies selected transcript text, otherwise it sends ETX to the active terminal. Ctrl+V sends clipboard text. Navigation keys use terminal escape sequences.\n- Resize is debounced and forwarded to ConPTY.\n- Transcript presentation is bounded to 250,000 characters and strips ANSI control sequences before display.\n\n## Shutdown and cleanup\n\nWindow closing is cancelled until `InteractiveTerminalSurface.DisposeAsync()` completes. This prevents the last-window shutdown path from abandoning an owned ConPTY session. Session close also cancels any queued resize operation before disposing the ConPTY session and awaiting the output pump. The underlying P08-004 kill-on-close job remains the authoritative owned-process cleanup mechanism.\n\n## Validation\n\n`tools/terminal/validate-interactive-terminal-ux.ps1` provides static, negative/recovery, and hosted Windows/WPF runtime composition/disposal coverage. It verifies the terminal composition seam, accessibility names, bounded transcript, input/interrupt mappings, resize forwarding, typed ConPTY use, and window-close disposal contract. The permanent Windows CI baseline invokes the validator, and `.github/workflows/p08-007-interactive-terminal-ux.yml` provides a dedicated path-scoped gate.\n\nNo owner-only evidence is required for P08-007. P08-008 remains separately pending until its own safety-test scope is selected and completed.\n''', encoding="utf-8", newline="\n")

Path("evidence/phases/P08/P08_007_CLOUD_IMPLEMENTATION_2026-09-07.md").write_text('''# FCCD-P08-007 — cloud implementation candidate\n\nSTATE: VALIDATION_PENDING\nTASK: FCCD-P08-007 — Interactive terminal UX\nBASE_MAIN: 596c43641b8f0706f27b96bfcb92cabb5859df62\nPR: #206\n\n## Implemented cloud scope\n\n- Existing P08 ConPTY host composed into the Bottom Tool Panel terminal seam.\n- PowerShell/CMD plus read-only detected Git Bash/WSL choices.\n- UTF-8 input/output, Ctrl+C interrupt/copy behavior, clipboard paste, navigation escape sequences.\n- Debounced ConPTY resize, bounded transcript, ANSI normalization, explicit Start/Close lifecycle.\n- Window shutdown is held until asynchronous terminal disposal completes; queued resize work is cancelled during close.\n- Permanent P08-007 static/negative/runtime validation and dedicated CI gate added.\n- Inherited P02 bottom-tool-panel validator repaired to accept property composition while preserving its existing removal negative fixture.\n\n## Initial failure recovered\n\nOriginal PR head `2b473fb6a25a8748eddc32aac461a823cc91b51f` built successfully with 0 warnings/0 errors and passed 174 unit plus 75 integration tests, but Windows CI #545, Workspace Search #274, and Large Workspace #258 failed at the inherited bottom-tool-panel validator because it required an exact self-closing `BottomToolPanelState` resource and rejected the legitimate `TerminalContent` property. This is a cloud-repairable CI contract defect and is repaired in this candidate; no gate is weakened.\n\n## Acceptance boundary\n\nThis file does not close the task and does not claim exact-head CI success. The candidate must pass the permanent Windows baseline, Workspace Search, Large Workspace Safeguards, and the dedicated P08-007 gate before normal merge. After merge, exact-main CI and canonical task reconciliation are still required. No owner/manual evidence is needed for this task. P08-008 and the P08 phase exit gate remain outside this task.\n''', encoding="utf-8", newline="\n")

